/usr/bin/bash -lc "cat > /tmp/codex-pr-508-review.md <<'EOF'
MUST-FIX

1. "'`src/cli/commands/session.ts:249`
   `computeUnlocksMap()` counts all dependents except `completed`/`cancelled`, but the linked spec `@session-start-unlocks` defines the annotation in terms of downstream `pending` tasks. This will overcount unlocks when a downstream task is `blocked`, `in_progress`, `needs_work`, or `pending_review`.

   Impact: agents/users may prioritize a task based on inflated unlock counts that include work already in progress or otherwise not pending.

   Recommended fix: count only dependents with `status === "pending"` (unless the spec is updated), and add a regression test for a non-pending dependent status.

